        "knowledge_base_version": "module5_authoritative_v1",
        "passage": "The FTC describes business-impersonator messages that appear to come from a familiar company but seek payment, personal information, or computer access. The guidance highlights unexpected contact, links or phone numbers supplied by the message, and hard-to-reverse payment demands. It recommends stopping and verifying the organization through trusted contact information.",
